Google has <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/gemini-on-apple-carplay/">announced</a> that a dedicated Gemini app on Apple CarPlay is rolling out around the world in several languages starting today, allowing you to have conversations with the AI assistant right from your vehicle's dashboard.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Google-Gemini-Apple-CarPlay.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076968" /><br/>
Gemini conversations on your iPhone automatically sync to CarPlay, so you can continue a previous conversation or start a new one.<br/>
<br/>
For example, you can ask Gemini to "Give me my daily brief for today" and it can give you a personalized answer based on your information in apps such as Gmail and Google Calendar. Or if you are driving around and looking for a restaurant, you could ask "What's a quick lunch spot in downtown Austin that's easy to get in and out of?"<br/>
<br/>
To get started, make sure you have the latest version of the Gemini app on your iPhone. Then, tap on the Gemini icon on CarPlay to start a conversation.<br/>
<br/>
CarPlay gained support for voice-based conversational AI apps starting with iOS 26.4. AI apps that have already rolled out CarPlay support include OpenAI's ChatGPT, Anthropic's Claude, X's Grok, Microsoft's Copilot, Perplexity, and others. iOS 27 also added Siri AI support to CarPlay, complete with a Siri app.<br/>
<br/>
